            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "creation_time": "2026-11-12T19:01:00Z",
            "text": "The JIT code cache is keyed on the function body. When a closure's body matches a cached one but jit_env_match() rejects the cached code, R_cmpfun() marks the closure NOJIT for good. That happens for an extra formal, a different top-level environment, an enclosing-frame variable the cached function lacked, or any hashed frame below the top-level environment, which new.env(), local() and sys.source(envir = new.env()) all create. Loops in such functions run 7-8x slower; an R6 method inherited by a subclass with private members is a common case. Separately, jit_env_match() never returns for an unhashed environment chain ending at emptyenv().\n\nReproducible example: attached as jit-cache-nojit-repro.R; it prints FALSE for the second function of each pair where TRUE (compiled) is expected, and its last call hangs.\n\nProposed patch: attached as jit-cache-nojit.diff, against r90880. It adds the formals and top-level environment to the cache key, accepts hashed frames, hashes the stored environment snapshots, stops the walks at the empty environment, and on a remaining conflict compiles for the union of both environments' variables (up to 256) instead of setting NOJIT. A regression test is included; make check passes on macOS.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/477, where CI results can be seen.",
            "bug_id": 19308,
            "count": 0,
            "is_markdown": false
          },
          {
            "bug_id": 19308,
            "text": "Created attachment 4044\nPatch against r90880: key the JIT cache on formals and top-level environment, recompile on conflicts instead of NOJIT",
            "is_markdown": false,
