          },
          {
            "text": "Created attachment 4048\nR6 reproducer: an inherited method stays uncompiled once the base class has compiled it\n\nA correction on the R6 case: private members aren't needed. Plain inheritance is enough, because R6 binds an extra `.__active__` in an inherited method's environment. Installed packages are affected too, since R6's `$new()` rebinds each method with `environment<-`, which drops the bytecode. Classes defined in a hashed environment (a Shiny app.R, a testthat test file, local()) fare worse: only the first object's methods are ever compiled.\n\nReproducer attached (r6-inherited-method-repro.R); it prints FALSE and a 6x slower time for the subclass's copy of the method. A workaround for the inheritance cases is proposed for R6 in https://github.com/r-lib/R6/pull/304; the hashed-environment case needs the fix in R.",
            "bug_id": 19308,
